# #5833. A PreArm append raises the partition's shared unstamped watermark, as a plain
# unstamped one does: every activation is told to replay past its own PreArm appends, so
# on a growing tree every armed leaf of the partition is held on the replay-based advance.
MODULE: PreArmCostWitnessSharedWatermark
TARGET: PreArmCostWitness
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a PreArm append raises the shared unstamped watermark
PERTURBS: PreArmAlloc

--- FIND
    /\ preArm' = preArm \cup {next}
    /\ seenU' = [seenU EXCEPT ![a] = Max2(@, ReportU)]
    /\ IF FreeOn THEN ReportForeign(a) ELSE UNCHANGED seenP
    /\ ReportStale(a)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, acked, floor, leafVars, epochVars, handVars>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<lastU, oldUsed, restarted, oldRejected, envVars>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ preArm' = preArm \cup {next}
\* MUTATION: the shared watermark is raised.
    /\ lastU' = next
    /\ seenU' = [seenU EXCEPT ![a] = Max2(@, next)]
    /\ IF FreeOn THEN ReportForeign(a) ELSE UNCHANGED seenP
    /\ ReportStale(a)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, acked, floor, leafVars, epochVars, handVars>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<oldUsed, restarted, oldRejected, envVars>>
--- END
